# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution): at 188 rad/s (300 mm/s) something fails; hv0.sim_dist,
# zeroed then, is how far the axis went (1 rad = 1.59 mm). Coasting takes
# ~16 rad (26 mm) and ~180 ms.
# The motor encoder fails (enc_fb0.sim_fail: a cut cable): no feedback, no
# quick stop; fb_stop = 2 (pmsm template) runs the dynamic brake: dbrake0
# shorts the motor through a virtual resistor in voltage mode, no angle
# needed (~3.8 rad, 6 mm; the bridge is off during the 1 ms the fault
# filter takes). The short current (~2 A, a transient up to ~5 A)
# stays under max_ac_cur (10 A), so rv stays 0. Then outputs off with mot
# FB error.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
hv0.sim_vel
hv0.sim_dist = 0
enc_fb0.sim_fail = 1
run 0.004
fault0.stop
@sample hv0.abs_cur 0.001 0.05
run 0.25
hv0.sim_dist
hv0.sim_vel
dbrake0.rv
fault0.fault
fault0.en_out
fault0.stop
@expect fault0.stop[1] == 2
@expect max|hv0.abs_cur| < 6
@expect hv0.sim_dist ~ 3.8 0.5
@expect hv0.sim_vel[2] ~ 0 0.5
@expect fault0.fault == 2
@expect fault0.en_out == 0
@expect fault0.stop[2] == 0
